The OP asked for personal opinions. I stated mine. I stand by it.

Everyone's favourite "Law Dwa Val" is just the combination that has
the most advantages built-in while it hardly has any disadvantages.
This makes it appear "easy" compared to other roles, because you can
play them straight-forward without having to be clever. One example:

Valks start with a +1 long sword, a good weapon, and lawfuls can dip
for Excalibur, an excellent weapon, very early on at XL:5. Now, both
weapons allow a "no thinking required" melee style -- just attack and
monsters die in 1-2 hits. Meleeing like that as a healer (+0 scalpel)
or archeologist (+0 pick-axe, +2 bullwhip) will fail, because those
weapons simply don't cause as much damage. That does *not* mean they
are "harder", just that people use the wrong strategy if they go valk
melee style with these roles.

That goes for nearly all elements of the game. You need to learn what
to do when and how, and what to avoid. Once you do that, role doesn't
matter.

